---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---
<Base title="Colophon" description="How this site is built and deployed.">
  <p class="crumb">~/colophon</p>
  <h1>Colophon</h1>
  <p>
    How this site is built and deployed. The source, including the infrastructure code, is on
    <a href={site.repo}>GitHub</a>.
  </p>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Stack</h2>
    <dl class="pairs">
      <dt>Site</dt><dd>Astro, built to static HTML with no client-side framework</dd>
      <dt>Hosting</dt><dd>Private S3 bucket behind CloudFront, using Origin Access Control</dd>
      <dt>DNS and TLS</dt><dd>Route 53 and an ACM certificate; domain registered with Porkbun</dd>
      <dt>Infrastructure</dt><dd>AWS CDK in TypeScript</dd>
      <dt>CI/CD</dt><dd>GitHub Actions, authenticating to AWS with OIDC; no long-lived keys</dd>
      <dt>Type</dt><dd>JetBrains Mono and Source Serif 4, self-hosted</dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Request path</h2>
    <pre><code>browser
  └─ dillon.isaacstse.dev      Route 53 alias record
       └─ CloudFront           TLS via ACM, CloudFront Function for redirects
            └─ S3 bucket       private, readable only by CloudFront</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <h2>Deploys</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>A push to main starts the pipeline.</li>
      <li>GitHub Actions builds the Astro site.</li>
      <li>The build is synced to S3.</li>
      <li>CloudFront's cache is invalidated.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>
</Base>
